      "source": "#42\n// array_builtins: range -> map -> filter -> sort -> reduce chain.\n// LFZ side uses the native higher-order builtins; the Python side uses the\n// equivalent native builtins (map/filter/sorted/functools.reduce) -- same algorithm.\n// Usage: the size N is read from stdin (one integer line).\nlet n = int(input())\nlet total = range(n) |> map((x) => x * 7 % n) |> filter((x) => x % 2 == 0) |> sort() |> reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)\nprint(\"RESULT total=${total}\")\n",
